Author: Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 23 15:38:00 2026 -0400

    refactor: port the tab page frame and root providers to frontend-base
    
    tab-page (TabPage, LoadedTabPage, TabWithTimer), the enrollment and
    logistration alerts, the user-messages and notices providers,
    PageLoading, the access helpers and the local-storage helper move to the
    same paths under frontend-base/src; the course tabs navigation, its slot
    and the header slot are dropped, since the shell renders the header and
    the course bar. Main.tsx mounts the three Learning-wide providers around
    the outlet. TabPage renders no header, footer or tour; LoadedTabPage no
    tabs, toolbar, streak modal or tours, and no second main-content id;
    TabWithTimer passes through to TabPage until the exam timer returns.
    Access-denied redirects are prefixed with the URL the learning role
    resolves to.
    
    The plugin override registry (generic/plugin-overrides) is dropped: on a
    frontend-base site no plugin can reach it, since the hook is not a
    package export and there is no slot to mount a widget in; its Slot API
    replacement is #2223.
    
    defaultProps become default parameters where the console hook met them,
    and react-fontawesome moves to 0.2.x, which has none. The package
    declares the FontAwesome and prop-types dependencies its files import.
    
    The package's lint config names src/**/*.jsx: frontend-base's base config
    lints no .jsx files (https://github.com/openedx/frontend-base/issues/327),
    and this commit brings the first.
    
    The package's coverage bar is not met at this commit: the alerts and the
    user-messages provider are exercised by the dates tab, which follows.
    
    Part of #2189.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

